==Finnish==

===Suffix===
'''-ton'''/'''-tön'''

# (''denominal'') Indicates lack of something, similar to [[-less]], [[in-]], [[im-]], [[il-]] and [[ir-]]; suffixed to the genitive singular stem of the noun.
:*Examples:
::*[[aika]] 'time' (genitive singular ''aja|<u>n</u>'') → [[ajaton]] 'timeless'
::*[[järki]] 'sense' (genitive singular ''järje|<u>n</u>'') → [[järjetön]] 'senseless'
::*[[maku]] 'taste' (genitive singular ''mau|<u>n</u>'') → [[mauton]] 'tasteless'
::*[[ääri]] 'border' (genitive singular ''ääre|<u>n</u>'') → [[ääretön]] 'infinite'

====Antonyms====
* [[-llinen]]

====Declension====
Inflected like [[Wiktionary:Finnish inflection types/nouns/onneton|onneton]] (back vowel harmony) or [[Wiktionary:Finnish inflection types/nouns/nimetön|nimetön]] (front vowel harmony).

